maya: FYI sampleapp rerank is showing strange embedding lengths after a retry path yesterday
kevin: what lengths?
maya: expected 1024 but some items are 1536. repro shows same inputs but the client merge created longer vectors
sam: any snippet of the merge code?
maya: yep, this was the culprit in the older node helper:
```
// bad: assumes partials are segments
function mergeResponses(base, partial) {
  return base.map((b, i) => {
    if (!partial[i]) return b;
    return b.concat(partial[i]);
  });
}
```
kevin: oof. concat will produce 1024+512 = 1536 if partials are different shape. Should replace or validate dims
alex: also noticed retries were missing a stable id header so SmartRouting occasionally sent a cheaper fallback variant on retry (different dim)
maya: quick fixes: replace concat with replacement, add dim check that throws on mismatch, and ensure idempotency headers (`x-batch-id` + `x-request-group`) are preserved across retries. PR: https://git.internal/redwood/sampleapp/pull/821
sam: for parity: python helper already raised on mismatch; node had older lenient behavior. I'll add a unit + e2e that injects a mismatched partial and asserts an error instead of corrupting output
ci-bot: pipeline queued: devex/embedding-batcher-dim-parity -> started
kevin: docs: add onboarding note clarifying response keys (embedding vs embeddings) and sample fix snippet for users
maya: added changelog entry under "embedding-batcher: stricter merge semantics" and a debug flag to log original batch ids + shapes
alex: assign sam for tests, maya for hotfix/docs, kevin for release notes. ETA tomorrow noon?
maya: works for me
kevin: thanks :thumbsup:
